 "duration": 229.041625,
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 5.76,
   "end": 23.08,
   "text": "I kept this close, so close to my heart Every evening I come home smiling"
  },
  {
   "start": 23.08,
   "end": 29.92,
   "text": "And I set my face like nothing's wrong You ask me, how was your day, ji?"
  },
  {
   "start": 30.46,
   "end": 36.92,
   "text": "And I say, fine, though I know it's not There is a room inside my chest"
  },
  {
   "start": 36.92,
   "end": 43.5,
   "text": "Where I keep the words I never said I wanted peace, I wanted time"
  },
  {
   "start": 43.5,
   "end": 51.74,
   "text": "I thought the truth could wait a while But the silence has a way tonight"
  },
  {
   "start": 51.74,
   "end": 58.84,
   "text": "And it follows me from room to room I stand at the edge of my own reply"
  },
  {
   "start": 59.66,
   "end": 68.62,
   "text": "Afraid of what comes into view I'm just tired, ji"
  },
  {
   "start": 68.62,
   "end": 74.62,
   "text": "Tired of holding what I can't undo I'm just tired, ji"
  },
  {
   "start": 75.58,
   "end": 81.72,
   "text": "Tired of pretending I can choose As you hear my voice shake a little"
  },
  {
   "start": 82.54,
   "end": 87.98,
   "text": "It's because I'm finally letting through I'm just tired, ji"
  },
  {
   "start": 89.26,
   "end": 93.26,
   "text": "And I need you to see me true"
  },
  {
   "start": 100.86,
   "end": 107.12,
   "text": "You found a letter on the table And the color left your face"
  },
  {
   "start": 107.12,
   "end": 113.76,
   "text": "I saw the hurt before the question It was standing in the space"
  },
  {
   "start": 113.76,
   "end": 120.38,
   "text": "I meant to tell you in the morning But my courage failed again"
  },
  {
   "start": 121.04,
   "end": 128.46,
   "text": "Now the truth is in the light And I cannot hide from it, my friend"
  },
  {
   "start": 132.28,
   "end": 140.38,
   "text": "I never meant to break your trust I never meant to turn away"
  },
  {
   "start": 140.38,
   "end": 144.94,
   "text": "But carrying this alone has worn my voice away"
  },
  {
   "start": 147.82,
   "end": 155.58,
   "text": "I'm just tired, ji Tired of living half a life"
  },
  {
   "start": 155.58,
   "end": 161.88,
   "text": "I'm just tired, ji Tired of cutting true to size"
  },
  {
   "start": 161.88,
   "end": 169.28,
   "text": "If my eyes look like they are begging It's because I don't know how to lie"
  },
  {
   "start": 169.28,
   "end": 177.12,
   "text": "I'm just tired, ji Please hear me before we say goodbye"
  },
  {
   "start": 181.32,
   "end": 188.68,
   "text": "Maybe love can hold the fracture Maybe truth can let us stay"
  },
  {
   "start": 188.68,
   "end": 194.96,
   "text": "If we walk through this together We may find a kinder way"
  },
  {
   "start": 197.82,
   "end": 205.34,
   "text": "I'm just tired, ji But I am still here by your side"
  },
  {
   "start": 205.9,
   "end": 211.82,
   "text": "I'm just tired, ji And I wanna make this right"
  },
  {
   "start": 211.82,
   "end": 219.26,
   "text": "If you can hold my hand for one more moment We can learn to breathe again tonight"
  },
  {
   "start": 219.26,
   "end": 227.04,
   "text": "I'm just tired, ji Stay with me now, let us begin again"
  }
 ],
